## 9. Add Interstitial Ads (After MCQ + After Experiment)

Interstitials are full-screen ads. In your final plan, you show them in **exactly two places**:
1. After completing an MCQ set
2. After finishing a virtual experiment

Both are natural break points where students expect a transition.

### Step 9.1 — Add a frequency cap (safety throttle)

Showing interstitials too frequently annoys students and triggers AdMob policy warnings. Cap them to **1 per 7 minutes per user** — this gives students a comfortable buffer between ads while still earning revenue from active users.

Create `artifacts/true-concept/src/lib/ad-frequency.ts`:

```typescript
import { showInterstitial } from "./admob";

const MIN_INTERVAL_MS = 7 * 60 * 1000;   // 7 minutes between interstitials
let lastShown = 0;

/**
 * Call this after MCQ set completion or experiment completion.
 * Shows an interstitial unless one was shown in the last 7 minutes
 * (keeps the app feeling friendly, not ad-spammy).
 */
export async function maybeShowInterstitial() {
  const now = Date.now();
  if (now - lastShown < MIN_INTERVAL_MS) {
    const minsLeft = Math.ceil((MIN_INTERVAL_MS - (now - lastShown)) / 60_000);
    console.info(`[AdMob] Skipped interstitial — next one in ${minsLeft} min`);
    return;
  }
  lastShown = now;
  await showInterstitial();
}
```

> **Why 7 minutes?** A typical student finishes one MCQ set in ~2-3 minutes and one experiment in ~5-10 minutes. With a 7-minute gap, fast students who rush through 3 MCQs in 5 minutes only see 1 ad — not 3 back-to-back. Slow students doing one activity at a time see an ad every time. Both feel respected.

### Step 9.2 — Trigger after MCQ completion

Find your MCQ completion logic in `pages/chapter-detail.tsx`:

