## 15. AdMob Policies — Don't Get Banned

Google bans 10–15% of new AdMob accounts in the first 6 months for policy violations. Here's how to **NOT** be one of them.

### Things that get you banned instantly

| Violation | Why It's Bad |
|---|---|
| ❌ Clicking your own ads (even once) | Invalid traffic — your account dies |
| ❌ Asking friends/family to click ads | Same as above — Google detects this |
| ❌ Buying clicks/impressions from a "service" | Same as above |
| ❌ Showing ads on illegal/copyrighted content | Policy violation |
| ❌ Showing ads to users under 13 without parental consent (COPPA) | Legal issue |
| ❌ Interstitial that shows on app launch (before user sees content) | Annoying users → banned |
| ❌ Banner placed where it can be accidentally clicked (like next to a button) | Accidental click violation |

### Things that get you banned slowly

| Issue | Why It's Bad |
|---|---|
| ⚠️ Interstitials every 30 seconds | Annoys users, low quality score |
| ⚠️ Misleading "Click to continue" labels next to ads | Deception |
| ⚠️ Hiding the close button on interstitials | Banned interaction pattern |
| ⚠️ Auto-refreshing banner faster than 30 sec | Earnings throttled |

### Safe practices

- ✅ Show banner at bottom of screen, far from interactive buttons
- ✅ Show interstitials at natural breaks (after activity, not during)
- ✅ Always clearly mark sponsored content if you have any
- ✅ Add your privacy policy URL to AdMob settings
- ✅ Read the policy: https://support.google.com/admob/answer/6128543

### Rule of thumb

> **If it would annoy YOU as a user, it'll get you banned.** Place ads with respect.

