## 16. Monitor Earnings

### Daily monitoring

After your app is live, check the AdMob dashboard daily for the first month:

1. Go to https://admob.google.com → **Home**
2. You'll see today's:
   - **Estimated earnings** (in INR)
   - **Impressions** (how many ads were shown)
   - **eCPM** (revenue per 1000 impressions)
   - **Match rate** (% of ad requests that returned an ad — should be >80%)
   - **Click-through rate (CTR)** (% of users who clicked — typical: 1-3%)

### Key metrics to watch

| Metric | Healthy Range | What It Means |
|---|---|---|
| Match rate | 80–100% | Higher = AdMob is filling your ad slots |
| Show rate | 90–100% | Higher = ads are actually displaying |
| eCPM (banner) | ₹25–₹85 | India education app range |
| eCPM (interstitial) | ₹85–₹250 | Higher because larger ad |
| eCPM (rewarded) | ₹400–₹850 | Highest because user opted in |
| CTR | 1–3% | Higher means users find ads relevant |

### A/B test placements

After 2-3 weeks of data, try moving the banner to the top vs bottom and see which earns more. AdMob's "Mediation" feature lets you A/B test automatically (advanced — explore later).

